meta {
  name: List Unlinked Households
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/clients/unlinked?kind=households&page=1&pageSize=25
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  kind: households
  page: 1
  pageSize: 25
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns a paginated envelope discriminated by kind", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.kind).to.equal("households");
    expect(body.items).to.be.an("array");
  });

  test("the envelope is internally consistent", function () {
    // Always runs, whatever the seed holds: a page never exceeds its own size,
    // and `totalPages` is derived from `total`, never reported independently.
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.items.length).to.be.at.most(body.pageSize);
    expect(body.totalPages).to.equal(
      Math.max(1, Math.ceil(body.total / body.pageSize)),
    );
  });

  test("agrees with the count on the chip", function () {
    const counted = bru.getVar("unlinkedHouseholdCount");
    if (counted !== undefined) {
      expect(res.getBody().total).to.equal(counted);
    }
  });

  test("every row carries the two signals that make it actionable", function () {
    const items = res.getBody().items;
    for (const row of items) {
      // How many people a primary could be picked from — 0 means "add a member
      // first", which is a different job.
      expect(row.memberCount).to.be.a("number");
      // 'no_primary' when somebody deliberately left it without one (§7),
      // null when nobody has looked. Both are in this one list.
      expect(
        row.dataQuality === null || row.dataQuality === "no_primary",
      ).to.equal(true);
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("primaryContactId");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("isTestRecord");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("agencyId");
    }
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /clients/unlinked?kind=households

  Households with **no primary contact** — 59 on the 2026-09-04 production data
  (PAC-91 §10).

  - **Module:** `clients`
  - **Permission:** `clients:read`
  - **Data scope:** `own` collapses to **branch**

  ## One list, not two
  Two situations satisfy "no primary contact", and this returns both:

  | `dataQuality` | Meaning |
  |---|---|
  | `"no_primary"` | Somebody **decided** to leave it without one (PAC-91 §7) — almost always a death with no successor |
  | `null` | Nobody has ever looked |

  They are one list because the predicate is the same, because `no_primary` is
  not a resolution (the answer is still "add a member and name them"), and
  because a count that disagreed with the database would undermine the one thing
  a data-quality list is for. The reason travels **on the row** so the UI can
  say which is which.

  This endpoint is the **only reader** `Household.dataQuality` has. It is
  projected, never used as a filter — which is why the field stays unindexed and
  Phase 5 ships no migration.

  ## Response
  `{ kind, page, pageSize, total, totalPages, items: UnlinkedHouseholdRow[] }`

  A row is `id`, `householdRef`, `name`, `status`, `city`, `state`,
  `totalActivePolicies`, `memberCount`, `dataQuality`, `createdAt`.

  - **`memberCount`** — **current** memberships (`endedAt: null`), the pool a
    primary can be named from. `0` means a member has to be added before anybody
    can lead the household, which is a different job from picking one, and it is
    the number that tells the two apart at a glance.
  - `city`/`state` come from `resolveHouseholdAddress`, which coerces the three
    writers' differing key shapes into one — never read `propertyAddress` raw.

  Rows exclude `isTestRecord` households.

  ## What the client does with a row
  Opens `/clients/:id` and uses **Change** on the primary-contact block —
  `POST /households/:id/primary-contact`, shipped in PAC-91 §7. This is the one
  kind whose fix is fully in the app already.

  ## Errors
  | Status | When |
  |---|---|
  | 400 | `kind` missing or outside the vocabulary, `page`/`pageSize` out of bounds |
  | 401 | Missing/expired bearer token |
  | 403 | `clients` disabled, or the caller lacks `clients:read` |
}
